Specifications implemented
  The compositing, adjustment, geometry and brush mathematics (docs/math/) are written from
  public specifications: the W3C "Compositing and Blending Level 1" recommendation, Adobe's
  public Photoshop File Formats Specification (PSD/PSB), the OpenRaster specification, and the
  PNG, JPEG and TIFF specifications. Where an algorithm is adapted from another free program
  (for example Krita or GIMP), the commit that adds it names the source and its license.

Test-only tools (not shipped)
  psd-tools (MIT) is used as an external cross-check of written PSD files and was read as a
  format reference, with provenance noted where used. GoogleTest (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy
  (BSD-3-Clause) and Pillow (MIT-CMU) run the test suite and are not distributed.

